{
  "name": "How to Choose the Right General Contractor for Your Project",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Picking the right general contractor can feel like a big decision, but it doesn't have to be overwhelming. You want someone who really understands your vision and can bring it to life without a hitch. First off, look for experience; have they tackled projects similar to yours before? That's a huge plus! Clear communication is another non-negotiable — you want someone who keeps you in the loop and is easy to talk to. Think about their availability, too. Can they start when you need them to, and will they be able to dedicate the time to your project? Don't forget to ask about their billing approach; knowing how payments are structured from the get-go avoids surprises. And always, always ask for references! A good contractor will happily provide them. They should also be able to handle permits, inspections, and coordinating all the different trades, like plumbing and electrical. When your project involves a lot of moving pieces or specific regulatory needs, choosing a qualified pro like HH Remodeling can save you a lot of headaches. Reach out to Abraham at 303-505-0866 for a chat about your next steps!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
